{
  "id": "ss.fx.vine-lash",
  "name": "Vine lash",
  "description": "One swing of a planted thicket, solved as a spiral about the plant it leaves. The radius grows with the angle rather than holding, because the tendril is still travelling outward when the swing runs out \u2014 a constant radius reads as a ring with a piece cut out of it, which is the first version of this and the reason for the second. Thick where it leaves the coil and drawn to a point, so the eye takes a direction off a shape that is on screen for a sixth of a second. The pivot is the document's own origin, which is why this box is square and mostly empty: the game drops the sprite on the thicket centre, turns it to the heading and scales it by the reach the weapon actually hits at, so the picture and the hitbox are the same number and no offset has to be carried in code. `meta.radius` is how far the tip gets from that pivot. Barbs lean back the way the swing came from and the leaf rides the tip, which is what sells a follow-through on a sprite that never moves.",
